{
  "section": "CRS-06",
  "name": "sender-certificate",
  "description": "Sender certificate parse and validation against one or more trust roots at a validation time (ms). Valid if and only if (a) some trust root verifies the server certificate signature, (b) the server key id is not revoked, (c) the server key verifies the sender certificate signature, and (d) validation_time <= expiration. Signatures are randomized XEdDSA: verify, do not compare. Certificate bodies were encoded from the CRS-06 table and signed with oracle keys; all results are oracle observations. Rejection reasons (fields named reason or error_if_*) are neutral paraphrases of the oracle result, not its text. The two signer-by-reference cases name the built-in production (id 3) and staging (id 2) server certificates and use the matching configured trust root: the reference resolves and the server certificate verifies under the trust root, but Comma holds no private key for those server keys, so the sender signature (made with a Comma key) does not verify and the certificate is invalid. No valid by-reference certificate can be produced without such a key.",
